/**
 * CRON → OWNING MANAGER — the last unmanaged surface, closed. Every schedule on the
 * dispatcher is RUN BY one of the 14 managers (the owner answers "why did this fire /
 * why didn't it"). Assignment follows the rails: a cron that drives one manager's rail
 * belongs to that manager; a cross-manager sweep (idle-hands, proactive-intelligence,
 * the whisper) belongs to the Data Steward, who owns orchestration. Aligned with
 * TABLE_MANAGER (a cron writing a manager's table is owned by that manager). The
 * manager-ownership guard derives the full path set from CRON_REGISTRY — adding a
 * cron without an owner here FAILS CI (same zero-orphan ratchet as tables/queues).
 */
